//
// Normative rule menvcfg_adue_op (src/priv/machine.adoc):
//   If the Svadu extension is implemented, the ADUE bit controls whether hardware updating of PTE
//     A/D bits is enabled for S-mode and G-stage address translations. When ADUE=1, hardware
//     updating of PTE A/D bits is enabled during S-mode address translation, and the implementation
//     behaves as though the Svade extension were not implemented for S-mode address translation.
//     When the hypervisor extension is implemented, if ADUE=1, hardware updating of PTE A/D bits is
//     enabled during G-stage address translation, and the implementation behaves as though the
//     Svade extension were not implemented for G-stage address translation. When ADUE=0, the
//     implementation behaves as though Svade were implemented for S-mode and G-stage address
//     translation.
//
// Context:
//   Tested in the Svadu suite because it defines Svadu's behavior. G-stage updating is in the H
//     suite (henvcfg_adue_op and the G-stage tests). The update scheme (<<translation>>, step 9): A
//     is set by any access, D by a store; D updates are exact, so a faulting store never sets D; A
//     and D are never cleared. S-mode translation covers S- and U-mode accesses through satp.
//     https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/3450: there are exactly two A/D schemes,
//     Svade and hardware updating; Svadu only adds menvcfg.ADUE to choose between them, and ADUE=0
//     means Svade (aswaterman: "!Svade && Svadu && ADUE=0 ... is actually not legal" as a third
//     behavior).
//
// Test plan:
//   ADUE=1: lw / fetch of an A=0 page succeed and set A (not D); sw of an A=0, D=0 page and of an
//     A=1, D=0 page succeed and set D and A; U-mode lw and sw likewise; a superpage leaf's A is
//     set; sw to an A=0, D=0 read-only page page-faults and leaves D=0.
//   ADUE=0: each of the S/U lw, fetch and sw cases page-faults (Svade) and the PTE is unchanged.
//
// Approximate dynamic instruction count: 4998
//

